# Self-loop avoidance under replacement: a flow whose two ends collapse
# to one item is dropped. Three ways to collapse: both ends in the
# group (A -> B), the replacer as target (A -> AB), the replacer as
# source (AB -> B). A genuine self-loop on an item that is not replaced
# (E -> E) is untouched. AB -> E shows the replacer still renders.

process A
process B
process E
process AB

A -> B   inside the group
A -> AB  to my replacer
AB -> B  from my replacer
E -> E   genuine self-loop
A -> E   out of the group

merge A B : AB
